# Advanced settings for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on one CMP 170HX card.
#
# You almost certainly don't need anything here: the common settings are in
# .env.example. ./start.sh reads only .env, so to use a setting from this
# file, copy its line into your .env (not into this file) and uncomment it.
# Every line shows the default the scripts use when it is unset, so a later
# release's new defaults reach you on ./start.sh update without editing .env.
# Delete or re-comment a line to go back to the default. The paths
# (/path/to/...) and HF_TOKEN lines are placeholders, not defaults; the note
# above each says what the default is.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, notes on their own lines starting with #.
# An unquoted value ends at the first " #" (whitespace then #), and a trailing
# "  (...)" (two or more spaces, then a note in parentheses) is dropped too.
# Quote the value, "..." or '...', to keep everything between the quotes.
# A prefix env assignment overrides .env for every key, including an
# explicit empty (KEY= ./start.sh):   MAX_SEQS=4 ./start.sh restart
#
# === paths ==============================================================
# Give an ABSOLUTE path when you move one. MODELS_DIR is in .env.example.
# The served checkpoint, built by ./start.sh download from the two below.
# Default: MODELS_DIR/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-3bpw-fp8ple.
# MODEL=/path/to/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-3bpw-fp8ple
#
# Weights to download: the 3 bpw checkpoint (without its BF16 n-gram table) and
# the FP8 table shards of the W4A16 one, repositories and pinned revisions.
# All three folders must be directly in MODELS_DIR (hard links).
# TARGET_REPO=klee100/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-AutoRound-3bpw-MTP
# TARGET_REVISION=ce0e0b94083895bd836b916f29bf105c40a8162a
# TABLE_REPO=halt95/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-Merlin
# TABLE_REVISION=cec53e9f90e5995b81691604ec0b32191debf797
# 1 copies instead of hard-linking when the folders are on different filesystems (~96 GiB).
# BUILD_COPY=
# CUDA graph mode: FULL_AND_PIECEWISE (default, the fast step), PIECEWISE, FULL.
# GRAPH_MODE=FULL_AND_PIECEWISE
# Unauthenticated Hub downloads are rate limited; a token is faster.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# 1 re-fetches the weights even when the files are already there.
# REFRESH_WEIGHTS=0
# === serving limits =====================================================
# Context is fixed at 262144 and GPU memory at 0.95: serve.sh refuses others.
# Concurrent sequences. 48 fit at 98 % of the KV pool with RecoverSSM; fewer
# keeps each user faster under load (docs/results.md).
# MAX_SEQS=48
# Parsers for Qwen's reasoning blocks and tool calls.
# REASONING_PARSER=qwen3
# TOOL_PARSER=qwen3_coder
# Extra vLLM arguments, whitespace-separated. Options that change the
# deployment (parallelism, dtype, context, graphs, speculation) are refused.
# EXTRA_ARGS=
# Seconds to wait for /health after launch.
# READY_TIMEOUT=1800
# 1 runs the post-start check (two requests, drafting active) after health.
# BOOT_CHECK=1
# Seconds stop waits for a clean shutdown.
# STOP_TIMEOUT=120
# === speculative decoding ===============================================
# dflash (inco.ai's DFlash 2 drafter, downloaded beside the checkpoint; the default),
# mtp (the native MTP head inside the checkpoint) or none.
# SPEC_MODE=dflash
# The drafter: repository and pinned revision.
# DRAFTER_REPO=incoai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2
# DRAFTER_REVISION=a22a1744e85c17364dcc54a6a420af7135d4c7f6
# Draft tokens per step: 7 for dflash (at most 7), 3 for mtp.
# SPEC_N=7
# mtp is the faster mode from about 16 users up, dflash for one to a few (docs/results.md, "MTP").
# Draft count by batch size (empty: off, SPEC_N drafts at every batch size):
# a JSON list of [first_batch,last_batch,drafts] ranges without spaces from
# batch 1. dflash default: [[1,2,7],[3,4,5],[5,48,3]]; mtp default: off (3 drafts
# at every batch size; fewer drafts under load did not help on one card). Set it
# empty (SPEC_SCHEDULE=) for SPEC_N drafts at every batch size.
# SPEC_SCHEDULE=
# === GDN layers =========================================================
# RecoverSSM: one recurrent state per request, accepted tokens replayed after sampling
# (1, the default); 0 = the engine's per-draft states (fewer requests fit).
# RECOVER_SSM=1
# GDN state precision: bfloat16 (default) or float32 (the checkpoint's).
# SSM_DTYPE=bfloat16
# Attention block size for dflash: a multiple of 48 at least the GDN state page;
# default 912 with bfloat16 states, 1680 with float32.
# BLOCK_SIZE=912
# === shared n-gram table ================================================
# The name of the shared table file in PLE_SHARED_DIR (.env.example); servers that
# share must use the same name and the same table.
# PLE_SHARED_NAME=qwen38-flash-next-ple-fp8
# === scheduler ==========================================================
# Tokens per scheduler step (prefill chunk plus decode slots).
# MAX_BATCHED=3460
# === n-gram (PLE) table ==================================================
# Where the n-gram table lives: ssd (default: read rows from the checkpoint
# file), or ram / device (comparison placements, not the tested default).
# PLE_PLACEMENT=ssd
# === container ==========================================================
# CONTAINER_NAME=qwen38-flash-next-1x
# SHM_SIZE=16g
# Default: cache/ in this repo.
# CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache
# === preflight ==========================================================
# Preflight limits (read only).
# MIN_GPUS=1
# MIN_GPU_MIB=61440
# NEED_DISK_GB=100
# === engine switches (kill switches: set 0 and restart) =================
# Canonical sparse-attention top-k ties: a request repeats at exact score ties.
# VLLM_QWEN4_QSA_TOPK_CANONICAL=1
# PLE row reads overlap the previous decoder layer instead of stalling the step.
# VLLM_EXL3_PLE_OVERLAP=1
# EXL3 MoE kernel v2 for MoE calls of 1-64 rows (decode and short prefills).
# VLLM_EXL3_MOE_V2=1
# EXL3 split-K dense kernel for the small-row decode launches.
# VLLM_EXL3_DENSE_SPLITK=1
# Tensor-core blocks for the split-K kernel's dense launches of 1-32 rows
# (needs VLLM_EXL3_DENSE_SPLITK).
# VLLM_EXL3_DENSE_MMA=1
# EXL3 tensor-core dense kernel for prefill launches of more than 64 rows.
# VLLM_EXL3_DENSE_PREFILL_TC=1
# EXL3 tensor-core MoE kernel for prefill MoE calls of 65-3460 rows.
# VLLM_EXL3_MOE_PREFILL_TC=1
# n-gram rows of a step read in one native call instead of a thread pool.
# VLLM_EXL3_PLE_NATIVE_READ=1
# Thin-M BF16 GEMM for the small-row calls of the unquantized projections.
# VLLM_THIN_GEMM=1
# Gluon thin GEMM for the decode shapes captured in CUDA graphs (needs VLLM_THIN_GEMM).
# VLLM_THIN_GEMM_GLUON=1
# FLA autotune skips configs that spill local memory (otherwise a first boot
# on a cold kernel cache loses KV cache space).
# VLLM_FLA_AUTOTUNE_SKIP_SPILLING=1
# Allocator.
# PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:False
# Opt-in device-specific compilation cache seed (container only).
# VLLM_IMAGE_CACHE_SEED=0
